nnective Tissue and its Heritable Disorders: Molecular, Genetic, and Medical aspects</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>New-York, Wiley-Liss</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Germain</surname><given-names>DP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ehlers-Danlos syndromes. Clinical, genetic and molecular aspects</article-title><source>Ann Dermatol Venereol</source><year>1995</year><volume>122</volume><fpage>187</fpage><lpage>204</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8526413</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Oderich</surname><given-names>GS</given-names></name><name><surname>Panneton</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Bower</surname><given-names>TC</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindor</surname><given-names>NM</given-names></name><name><surname>Cherry</surname><given-names>KJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Noel</surname><given-names>AA</given-names></name><name><surname>Kalra</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sullivan</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Gloviczki</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The spectrum, management and clinical outcome of Ehlers-Danlos syndrome type IV: a 30-year experience</article-title><source>J Vasc Surg</source><year>2005</year><volume>42</volume><fpage>98</fpage><lpage>106</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16012458</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.jvs.2005.03.053</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Karkos</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name><name><surname>Prasad</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Mukhopadhyay</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomson</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Hearn</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Rupture of the abdominal aorta in patients with Ehlers-Danlos syndrome</article-title><source>Ann Vasc Surg</source><year>2000</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>274</fpage><lpage>277</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10796961</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1007/s100169910047</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cikrit</surname><given-names>DF</given-names></name><name><surname>Miles</surname><given-names>JH</given-names></name><name><surname>Silver</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Spontaneous arterial perforation: the Ehlers-Danlos specter</article-title><source>J Vasc Surg</source><year>1987</year><volume>5</volume><fpage>248</fpage><lpage>255</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3546738</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1067/mva.1987.avs0050248</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mattar</surname><given-names>SG</given-names></name><name><surname>Kumar</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name><name><surname>Lumsden</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Vascular complications in Ehlers-Danlos syndrome</article-title><source>Am Surg</source><year>1994</year><volume>60</volume><fpage>827</fpage><lpage>831</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7978674</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Freeman</surname><given-names>RK</given-names></name><name><surname>Swegle</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Sise</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The surgical complications of Ehlers-Danlos syndrome</article-title><source>Am Surg</sourc